From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:02:59 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] port 6d513178 096efada: fused_gr: STRATA_GR_DOWN_PF=2|3
 keeps 2 or 3 tiles of weights in flight in the staged down projection
 (opt-in)

gr_down_staged_kernel with the weights of PF tiles in flight instead of one: the eight tiles are unrolled, so a
lane's weights sit in a ring of PF + 1 register slots at compile-time indices.  The activations' staging, the
barriers and every sum are the staged kernel's, so the same bits.  Only for the exact-token launches of 1..6 tokens.
ctests gr_parity_down_pf2 / _pf3 (STRATA_HC_SPLIT=2), with b628d059's 1..7-token comparison.  096efada (the kernel's
header comment reworded) folded in.  TESTLOG #77: the gr arm (GR_FAST + PF2 + NORM_FAST) +1.4/+1.8 % HTTP.

(cherry picked from commits 6d5131783ffc and 096efada85f2)

Port to v0.2.12:
- ported in the pre-split form (no DOWN_SPLIT ROWS template from the dropped 0bf42041).
- v0.2.12's staged kernel gained token groups on gridDim.y (down_tg, STRATA_GR_DOWN_TG; default only on sm_75 and
  12.0 cards, 0 on sm_86).  The PF kernel keeps one block row for all tokens, so it runs only where the launch is
  not split into token groups: split_tg first (upstream's branch unchanged), then pf, then the exact-T chain.
  With STRATA_GR_DOWN_PF unset (pf = 1) the launch chain is upstream's.
- GR_V3 (another read, its own kernels) and GR_UP_WIDE (the up projection, after the down) are untouched; PF only
  applies when the staged read is the one that runs (sm_86: v3 off by default).
- fused_gr_bench header note; gr_parity_norm_fast is not carried (upstream's fec7d1ca has its own form).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
